0
00:00:07,211 --> 00:00:09,247
PREVIOUSLY ON
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL,"

1
00:00:09,247 --> 00:00:10,515
JOANIE TOUGHED IT OUT
IN THE DENTIST CHAIR...

2
00:00:10,515 --> 00:00:11,916
WOW.

3
00:00:11,916 --> 00:00:13,919
AND CAME AWAY
WITH SOMETHING TO SMILE ABOUT.

4
00:00:13,919 --> 00:00:16,354
MY PLEASURE, MY PLEASURE.

5
00:00:16,354 --> 00:00:18,423
WHILE DANIELLE HUNG ON
TO HER GAP TOOTH GRIN...

6
00:00:18,423 --> 00:00:20,158
THE GAP, I-I LOVE THE GAP.

7
00:00:20,158 --> 00:00:21,460
AND THE DARK SIDE
OF MODELING

8
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:24,262
CALLED FOR A SHOOT
FILLED WITH BEAUTY AND TEARS...

9
00:00:24,262 --> 00:00:26,398
KEEP IT SAD.

10
00:00:26,398 --> 00:00:28,700
BUT BROOKE COULDN'T
BRING EMOTION TO HER SHOOT.

11
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:30,902
FOR A GIRL WHO CRIES A LOT,

12
00:00:30,902 --> 00:00:32,571
I THINK THAT COULD HAVE BEEN
A STRONGER PICTURE.

13
00:00:32,571 --> 00:00:33,839
AND SHE WAS SENT HOME.

14
00:00:33,839 --> 00:00:35,407
SIX GIRLS REMAIN.

15
00:00:35,407 --> 00:00:38,275
WHO WILL BE ELIMINATED TONIGHT?

16
00:00:38,275 --> 00:00:46,184
♪♪♪

17
00:01:22,043 --> 00:01:25,757
♪♪♪

18
00:01:25,757 --> 00:01:27,959
(laughs)
STOP.

19
00:01:27,959 --> 00:01:30,662
(sighs)
I HAVE ONLY ONE PICTURE LEFT.

20
00:01:30,662 --> 00:01:35,534
WHO IS
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL?

21
00:01:35,534 --> 00:01:37,335
FURONDA.

22
00:01:37,335 --> 00:01:39,604
THANK YOU FOR BELIEVING
IN ME.

23
00:01:39,604 --> 00:01:43,441
(laughs)

24
00:01:43,441 --> 00:01:45,844
JADE IS MY FAVORITE PERSON
IN THE HOUSE.

25
00:01:45,844 --> 00:01:46,978
THAT ONE...

26
00:01:46,978 --> 00:01:48,280
OR THIS ONE?

27
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:50,348
(laughs)

28
00:01:50,348 --> 00:01:53,552
JADE AND NNENNA SEEMED LIKE
TWO OPPOSITE PEOPLE TO ME,

29
00:01:53,552 --> 00:01:55,520
BUT AS I'VE BEEN
GETTING TO KNOW BOTH OF THEM,

30
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:57,322
I DO SEE A LOT OF SIMILARITIES.

31
00:01:57,322 --> 00:01:59,224
I WOULD LIKE
TO WORK WITH JADE SOMEDAY.

32
00:01:59,224 --> 00:02:00,292
AND I'D LIKE TO WORK
WITH NNENNA.

33
00:02:00,292 --> 00:02:01,726
JADE AND I
HAVE FORMED A FRIENDSHIP

34
00:02:01,726 --> 00:02:03,562
EVEN THOUGH IT IS A COMPETITION.

35
00:02:03,562 --> 00:02:05,597
(laughs)

36
00:02:05,597 --> 00:02:09,768
WE JUST SEE IT AS
"MAY THE BEST PERSON WIN."

37
00:02:09,768 --> 00:02:12,704
THIS COMPETITION, FOR ME,
IS LOOKIN' UP.

38
00:02:12,704 --> 00:02:14,906
WHOO.

39
00:02:14,906 --> 00:02:16,975
MY PICTURES
ARE GETTIN' BETTER AND BETTER,

40
00:02:16,975 --> 00:02:18,610
THE JUDGES ARE
TAKING NOTICE OF ME.

41
00:02:18,610 --> 00:02:20,478
I WASN'T SURE
YOU WERE PHOTOGENIC,

42
00:02:20,478 --> 00:02:22,714
AND AS THE WEEKS HAVE GONE ON,
YOU'VE JUST GROWN.

43
00:02:22,714 --> 00:02:24,182
AND THAT IS WHAT

44
00:02:24,182 --> 00:02:24,883
WE'RE LOOKING FOR OFTEN
IN A TOP MODEL--

45
00:02:24,883 --> 00:02:26,518
SOMEONE THAT DEVELOPS.

46
00:02:26,518 --> 00:02:27,886
I'M BEGINNING
TO BE A FORERUNNER

47
00:02:27,886 --> 00:02:30,255
IN THIS COMPETITION,
AND IT'S SETTING ME ON A PATH

48
00:02:30,255 --> 00:02:32,524
TO WIN, WIN, WIN, WIN, WIN.

49
00:02:32,524 --> 00:02:35,694
OOH, MY LEGS IS BURNIN',
MY JOINTS, MY HIPS.

50
00:02:39,264 --> 00:02:40,966
THE COMPETITION
IS GETTING REALLY SERIOUS,

51
00:02:40,966 --> 00:02:44,502
AND TYRA ASKED ME TO GET
THE GAP IN MY TEETH CLOSED.

52
00:02:44,502 --> 00:02:47,305
EASY, BREEZY,
BEAUTIFUL COVERGIRL.

53
00:02:47,305 --> 00:02:48,874
DO YOU REALLY THINK YOU CAN
HAVE A COVERGIRL CONTRACT

54
00:02:48,874 --> 00:02:49,808
WITH THE GAP IN YOUR MOUTH?

55
00:02:49,808 --> 00:02:50,842
YES, WHY NOT?

56
00:02:50,842 --> 00:02:52,477
THIS IS ALL PEOPLE SEE.

57
00:02:52,477 --> 00:02:53,612
IT'S EASY, BREEZY,
BEAUTIFUL COVERGIRL.

58
00:02:53,612 --> 00:02:55,247
IT'S NOT MARKETABLE.

59
00:02:55,247 --> 00:02:56,481
I DON'T WANNA GO HOME

60
00:02:56,481 --> 00:02:57,949
BECAUSE I DIDN'T GET
THE GAP CLOSED.

61
00:03:05,190 --> 00:03:07,492
I HAVE TO CHOOSE MY GAP
OR GOIN' HOME,

62
00:03:07,492 --> 00:03:09,261
AND I'M AT THE BOTTOM RIGHT NOW.

63
00:03:09,261 --> 00:03:10,762
I FEEL LIKE THAT IS
THE BIGGEST CHALLENGE

64
00:03:10,762 --> 00:03:12,764
THAT HAS EVER FACED ME.

65
00:03:12,764 --> 00:03:13,765
TYRA MAIL.

66
00:03:13,765 --> 00:03:14,799
TYRA MAIL.

67
00:03:14,799 --> 00:03:15,800
TYRA MAIL.

68
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,202
TYRA MAIL.

69
00:03:17,202 --> 00:03:18,970
"HOW PRESSED ARE YOU TO WIN?

70
00:03:18,970 --> 00:03:20,572
"FIND OUT IF YOU CAN
HANDLE THE STRESS.

71
00:03:20,572 --> 00:03:23,575
TYRA."

72
00:03:23,575 --> 00:03:29,281
♪♪♪

73
00:03:33,551 --> 00:03:35,487
HI, I'M RACHEL McCALLISTER,

74
00:03:35,487 --> 00:03:37,188
AND I'M A PARTNER
AND CO-FOUNDER

75
00:03:37,188 --> 00:03:39,357
IN MPRM PUBLIC RELATIONS.

76
00:03:39,357 --> 00:03:42,761
AT THE AGENCY, MY ROLE IS
TO HELP MEDIA-TRAIN OUR CLIENTS,

77
00:03:42,761 --> 00:03:44,329
AND THAT MEANS HELPING THEM

78
00:03:44,329 --> 00:03:46,464
TO DO A REALLY
EFFECTIVE INTERVIEW.

79
00:03:46,464 --> 00:03:48,366
RACHEL McCALLISTER--
SHE'S GIVIN' US

80
00:03:48,366 --> 00:03:50,568
THE DO'S AND DON'TS
OF DEALING WITH THE PRESS.

81
00:03:50,568 --> 00:03:53,371
DON'T BE SURPRISED
IF SOMEBODY COMES UP TO YOU

82
00:03:53,371 --> 00:03:56,274
AND SAYS, "OH, SO I HEAR
YOUR FATHER'S REALLY HORRIFIED

83
00:03:56,274 --> 00:03:58,310
BY THE FACT THAT
YOU'RE DOING THIS SHOOT

84
00:03:58,310 --> 00:03:59,678
WHERE YOU GOTTA
TAKE YOUR CLOTHES OFF.

85
00:03:59,678 --> 00:04:01,913
WHAT YOU WANNA DO IS SAY,
"WELL, THAT'S AN AREA

86
00:04:01,913 --> 00:04:05,417
THAT IS OF CONCERN TO HIM,
BUT HE'S REALLY SUPPORTIVE."

87
00:04:05,417 --> 00:04:06,985
FOCUS ON THE POSITIVE.

88
00:04:06,985 --> 00:04:09,854
YOU'RE GONNA BE ASKED
A LOT OF VERY TOUGH QUESTIONS

89
00:04:09,854 --> 00:04:12,590
LIKE, "I HEAR YOUR BOYFRIEND
CAUGHT YOU WITH ANOTHER GUY."

90
00:04:12,590 --> 00:04:13,858
(laughs)

91
00:04:13,858 --> 00:04:15,493
WHAT WAS THAT ALL ABOUT?

92
00:04:15,493 --> 00:04:17,529
LAST FRAME.

93
00:04:17,529 --> 00:04:19,464
WORK, DAMN IT.

94
00:04:19,464 --> 00:04:22,667
I-I THINK EVERYTHING
IS GONNA BE FINE.

95
00:04:22,667 --> 00:04:24,202
OH, GOD.

96
00:04:24,202 --> 00:04:26,237
I INADVERTENTLY
HIT THE JACKPOT.

97
00:04:26,237 --> 00:04:29,374
HAVING NO CLUE THAT APPARENTLY,
THAT MUST HAVE HAPPENED.

98
00:04:29,374 --> 00:04:32,277
THIS IS CLEARLY THE ONE QUESTION
YOU DIDN'T WANT ASKED.

99
00:04:32,277 --> 00:04:33,511
YEAH.

100
00:04:33,511 --> 00:04:34,713
KNOW THAT
IT'S GONNA BE ASKED.

101
00:04:34,713 --> 00:04:37,816
THEY ALL SEEMED TO UNDERSTAND
WHAT I WAS SAYING.

102
00:04:37,816 --> 00:04:40,185
OF COURSE, THE TRUTH
WILL BE IN THE CHALLENGE,

103
00:04:40,185 --> 00:04:43,254
BECAUSE I'M NEVER GONNA BE
AS TOUGH AS A REPORTER.

104
00:04:43,254 --> 00:04:46,491
TODAY I'VE SET UP AN INTERVIEW
WITH COLUMNIST GEORGE WAYNE.

105
00:04:46,491 --> 00:04:49,327
GEORGE WILL BE JUDGING YOU
ON TWO ISSUES--

106
00:04:49,327 --> 00:04:52,664
ONE ON HOW EFFECTIVELY
YOU ANSWER HIS QUESTIONS,

107
00:04:52,664 --> 00:04:55,300
AND TWO, HOW WELL
YOU PRESENT YOURSELF.

108
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:56,334
GOOD LUCK.

109
00:04:56,334 --> 00:04:57,736
MY NAME IS GEORGE WAYNE.

110
00:04:57,736 --> 00:04:59,671
IF YOU'VE NEVER HEARD
OF MY NAME BEFORE THIS MOMENT,

111
00:04:59,671 --> 00:05:01,673
YOU WON'T FORGET IT
BEFORE THE END OF THIS EVENING.

112
00:05:01,673 --> 00:05:02,674
YOU READY?

113
00:05:02,674 --> 00:05:03,908
YES.

114
00:05:03,908 --> 00:05:05,877
WHAT MADE YOU CONSIDER
A CAREER IN MODELING?

115
00:05:05,877 --> 00:05:07,379
DO YOU THINK
YOU PHOTOGRAPH VERY WELL?

116
00:05:07,379 --> 00:05:08,380
YES.

117
00:05:08,380 --> 00:05:09,647
EVEN THOUGH
I CAN PLAY WITH MY AGE,

118
00:05:09,647 --> 00:05:11,449
I CAN PLAY WITH
MY VERSATILITY OF LOOKS.

119
00:05:11,449 --> 00:05:12,884
WHEN I INTERVIEW CELEBRITIES,

120
00:05:12,884 --> 00:05:15,620
I GO FOR THE JUGULAR
IN A GOOD WAY.

121
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:16,755
RELAX A LITTLE BIT.
YOU'RE A LITTLE STIFF.

122
00:05:16,755 --> 00:05:17,789
SIT BACK.

123
00:05:17,789 --> 00:05:19,324
WHAT'S WITH THE HEAD WRAP?

124
00:05:19,324 --> 00:05:20,625
IT'S JUST THE JADE STYLE.

125
00:05:20,625 --> 00:05:22,527
YOU LOOK LIKE
AN ARROGANT BITCH TO ME.

126
00:05:22,527 --> 00:05:23,661
I'M SORRY?

127
00:05:23,661 --> 00:05:25,230
DO YOU THINK
YOU'RE ANITA SIMONE?

128
00:05:25,230 --> 00:05:27,699
THIS IS SOMETHING, GEORGE,
I'VE BEEN TRYING TO DEFEAT,

129
00:05:27,699 --> 00:05:29,868
BECAUSE I'M JUST VERY
DOWN TO EARTH, I'M VERY COOL.

130
00:05:29,868 --> 00:05:31,703
I'M AN EXOTIC
BIRACIAL BUTTERFLY.

131
00:05:31,703 --> 00:05:32,804
(laughs)
EXOTIC BIRACIAL BUTTERFLY.

132
00:05:32,804 --> 00:05:34,205
YES.

133
00:05:34,205 --> 00:05:35,373
- INTERESTING.
- YES.

134
00:05:35,373 --> 00:05:37,542
I AM NOT AFRAID TO ASK
THE TOUGH QUESTION.

135
00:05:37,542 --> 00:05:39,811
IT'S MY JOB,
AND I THRIVE ON IT.

136
00:05:39,811 --> 00:05:41,946
WHAT WOULD YOU CONSIDER
YOUR WORST ATTRIBUTE?

137
00:05:41,946 --> 00:05:42,881
I'M VERY STUBBORN.

138
00:05:42,881 --> 00:05:44,349
IT RUNS IN THE FAMILY.

139
00:05:44,349 --> 00:05:45,517
I'M VERY,
VERY CANTANKEROUS.

140
00:05:45,517 --> 00:05:46,518
SPELL THE WORD.

141
00:05:46,518 --> 00:05:47,852
- "CANTANKEROUS"?
- YEAH.

142
00:05:47,852 --> 00:05:50,622
I'M NOT EXACTLY SURE
HOW TO SPELL "CANTANKEROUS."

143
00:05:50,622 --> 00:05:52,791
WOULD YOU GIVE UP
YOUR BOYFRIEND FOR YOUR CAREER?

144
00:05:52,791 --> 00:05:54,192
IN MY OPINION,

145
00:05:54,192 --> 00:05:55,627
I FEEL LIKE IT WOULDN'T
BE ALL OR NOTHING FOR ME

146
00:05:55,627 --> 00:05:58,496
JUST BECAUSE I FEEL A REAL
STRENGTH IN THAT RELATIONSHIP.

147
00:05:58,496 --> 00:05:59,831
UNDO YOUR HAIR.
LET ME SEE.

148
00:05:59,831 --> 00:06:01,433
- GIVE ME A LITTLE...
- (laughs)

149
00:06:01,433 --> 00:06:02,600
LIKE, AAH.

150
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:03,968
LET ME SEE IF YOU HAVE
ANY SEXINESS TO YOU.

151
00:06:03,968 --> 00:06:04,969
I'M NOT SEXY?

152
00:06:04,969 --> 00:06:05,970
NOT REALLY.

153
00:06:05,970 --> 00:06:07,038
IS MY HAIR PRETTY, THOUGH?

154
00:06:07,038 --> 00:06:08,573
PRETTY HAIR.

155
00:06:08,573 --> 00:06:09,908
YOU THINK
YOU'RE THE QUEEN OF SHEBA?

156
00:06:09,908 --> 00:06:11,342
NO, I'VE NEVER BEEN TO SHEBA.

157
00:06:11,342 --> 00:06:12,777
I'VE NEVER BEEN TO SHEBA.

158
00:06:12,777 --> 00:06:13,978
DO YOU THINK SO?

159
00:06:13,978 --> 00:06:15,213
YEAH,
YOU'RE A SHEBA LIONESS.

160
00:06:15,213 --> 00:06:16,247
(imitates roaring)

161
00:06:16,247 --> 00:06:17,248
ROAR FOR ME.

162
00:06:17,248 --> 00:06:18,583
(imitates roaring)

163
00:06:18,583 --> 00:06:19,784
WHAT WOULD YOU CONSIDER

164
00:06:19,784 --> 00:06:22,687
THE MOST AMAZING
PHYSICAL ASSET THAT YOU POSSESS?

165
00:06:22,687 --> 00:06:23,688
MY SMILE.

166
00:06:23,688 --> 00:06:25,557
MOST PEOPLE
RECOGNIZE MY SMILE.

167
00:06:25,557 --> 00:06:26,858
I'M DUMBSTRUCK.

168
00:06:26,858 --> 00:06:28,193
YOU'RE DUMBSTRUCK?

169
00:06:28,193 --> 00:06:28,793
I'M SURE YOU GET THAT
ALL THE TIME.

170
00:06:28,793 --> 00:06:30,195
WHY IS THAT?

171
00:06:30,195 --> 00:06:30,795
YOU'RE A GAZELLE.

172
00:06:30,795 --> 00:06:31,796
WHY DO YOU SAY THAT?

173
00:06:31,796 --> 00:06:32,797
YOU'RE A SNOB.

174
00:06:32,797 --> 00:06:33,798
REALLY?

175
00:06:33,798 --> 00:06:35,200
MM.

176
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,401
I DON'T THINK SO.

177
00:06:36,401 --> 00:06:37,302
JUST BY YOUR REACTION,
I CAN TELL.

178
00:06:37,302 --> 00:06:38,636
NO, I'M NOT SNOBBISH.

179
00:06:38,636 --> 00:06:39,871
WHAT IS THE ONE THING
YOU WANT THE WORLD

180
00:06:39,871 --> 00:06:41,339
TO KNOW ABOUT YOU?

181
00:06:41,339 --> 00:06:42,874
I HAVE A BIG FAMILY
IN AFRICA,

182
00:06:42,874 --> 00:06:45,577
AND I THINK HAVING FAIR TRADE
IN AFRICA WOULD HELP THEM.

183
00:06:45,577 --> 00:06:47,245
YOU SOUND LIKE
A MISS WORLD CONTESTANT.

184
00:06:47,245 --> 00:06:48,813
NO, IT'S NOT LIKE I HAVE--

185
00:06:48,813 --> 00:06:50,582
THIS IS NOT
MISS UNIVERSE PAGEANT.

186
00:06:50,582 --> 00:06:52,717
NNENNA IS A BIG PRESENCE,
VERY SMART.

187
00:06:52,717 --> 00:06:55,854
YOU CAN TELL THAT
SHE IS A VERY COMPLEX CREATURE.

188
00:06:55,854 --> 00:06:57,222
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

189
00:06:57,222 --> 00:06:58,389
IT'S NICE TO MEET YOU.

190
00:06:58,389 --> 00:06:59,757
I WAS HERE TO JUDGE
ON A CERTAIN LEVEL

191
00:06:59,757 --> 00:07:04,696
THE GRACE, THE CHARACTER,
THE PRESENCE OF EACH GIRL.

192
00:07:04,696 --> 00:07:06,698
GIRLS, I WANT
TO THANK ALL OF YOU.

193
00:07:06,698 --> 00:07:08,333
WHAT I WANNA DO
IS TELL YOU WHAT I LIKED

194
00:07:08,333 --> 00:07:10,268
AND WHAT WE PROBABLY COULD
WORK ON A LITTLE BIT.

195
00:07:10,268 --> 00:07:11,636
SO I'LL START WITH FURONDA.

196
00:07:11,636 --> 00:07:13,605
YOU HANDLED A TOUGH SESSION,

197
00:07:13,605 --> 00:07:15,740
AS IT WERE, AND I THOUGHT
YOU DID VERY WELL.

198
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:18,910
JOANIE, OF ALL THE GIRLS TODAY,
YOU WERE THE TRUEST.

199
00:07:18,910 --> 00:07:20,278
I THINK YOU'RE SPECIAL.

200
00:07:20,278 --> 00:07:22,514
DANIELLE, I THINK
YOU HAVE A GREAT PRESENCE,

201
00:07:22,514 --> 00:07:26,484
BUT YOU NEED TO,
UH, IMPROVE YOUR SPEECH.

202
00:07:26,484 --> 00:07:28,419
SARA, SMART GIRL,

203
00:07:28,419 --> 00:07:29,854
BUT I'M NOT REALLY SURE
IF THIS IS REALLY

204
00:07:29,854 --> 00:07:31,422
WHAT YOU WANT TO DO.

205
00:07:31,422 --> 00:07:32,857
I HAVE TO FIGURE OUT
WHAT I'M DOING

206
00:07:32,857 --> 00:07:35,560
THAT IS MAKING PEOPLE THINK
I DON'T REALLY WANT THIS,

207
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:36,628
AND I HAVE TO
FIX THAT IMMEDIATELY.

208
00:07:36,628 --> 00:07:39,497
NNENNA, YOU HANDLED YOURSELF
WELL UNDER PRESSURE.

209
00:07:39,497 --> 00:07:41,199
SOMETIMES I THINK
YOU'RE A LITTLE SNOBBY,

210
00:07:41,199 --> 00:07:43,368
BUT, UH, YOU'RE QUITE GOOD.

211
00:07:43,368 --> 00:07:44,769
JADE, GIVE ME
THOSE DAGGER EYES.

212
00:07:44,769 --> 00:07:46,404
RELAX A LITTLE BIT.

213
00:07:46,404 --> 00:07:48,373
DON'T TAKE ON
YOUR INTERVIEWEE.

214
00:07:48,373 --> 00:07:49,574
A LITTLE HUMILITY
GOES A LONG WAY.

215
00:07:49,574 --> 00:07:55,313
ANYWAY, I CAN ONLY CHOOSE
ONE GIRL.

216
00:07:55,313 --> 00:07:58,683
IT'S REALLY TOUGH FOR ME,
BUT I'M GONNA GO WITH NNENNA.

217
00:07:58,683 --> 00:08:00,351
(applause)

218
00:08:00,351 --> 00:08:02,387
THANK YOU.

219
00:08:02,387 --> 00:08:04,489
YOU GAVE A GREAT INTERVIEW,
AND I THINK YOU HAVE

220
00:08:04,489 --> 00:08:07,625
IMMENSE POTENTIAL TO BE PROBABLY
THE BEST TOP MODEL EVER.

221
00:08:07,625 --> 00:08:09,360
I THINK NNENNA'S
HITTING THE NAIL ON THE HEAD

222
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,495
PRETTY CONSISTENTLY.

223
00:08:10,495 --> 00:08:11,696
I'M JUST GONNA
HAVE TO WORK HARDER

224
00:08:11,696 --> 00:08:13,965
TO TRY TO BEAT NNENNA OUT
AT THE NEXT ONE.

225
00:08:13,965 --> 00:08:15,466
YOU'LL BE GETTIN'
A SPA TREATMENT,

226
00:08:15,466 --> 00:08:17,435
ALL EXPENSES PAID,
AND YOU GET TO CHOOSE

227
00:08:17,435 --> 00:08:18,970
ONE OF THESE LOVELY LADIES
TO GO WITH.

228
00:08:18,970 --> 00:08:20,672
JADE.

229
00:08:20,672 --> 00:08:23,942
JADE AND NNENNA
HAVE WON SIX TIMES.

230
00:08:23,942 --> 00:08:25,877
YOU JUST GET SICK
OF THEM WINNING.

231
00:08:25,877 --> 00:08:27,445
AND THE REST OF YOU GIRLS

232
00:08:27,445 --> 00:08:29,314
ARE GOING TO HAVE TO CATER
TO THESE LOVELY WINNERS.

233
00:08:29,314 --> 00:08:30,748
THE GIRLS
HAVE A RIGHT TO BE MAD

234
00:08:30,748 --> 00:08:33,418
THAT THEY KEEP NOT WINNIN',
BUT THIS IS A COMPETITION.

235
00:08:33,418 --> 00:08:34,752
WHAT DO YOU EXPECT?

236
00:08:34,752 --> 00:08:36,821
SOMEBODY'S GOTTA WIN,
AND SOMEBODY'S GOTTA LOSE.

237
00:08:36,821 --> 00:08:38,389
I REALLY ENJOYED
MEETING ALL OF YOU,

238
00:08:38,389 --> 00:08:39,824
AND YOU ALL HAVE SOMETHING
REALLY SPECIAL.

239
00:08:39,824 --> 00:08:42,860
NICE TO MEET YOU, TOO.

240
00:08:49,967 --> 00:08:52,403
I THINK THAT DANIELLE
NOW SEES HER GAP AS SOMETHING

241
00:08:52,403 --> 00:08:56,307
THAT MAKES HER UNIQUE,
BECAUSE IT'S KIND OF SIGNATURE.

242
00:09:02,747 --> 00:09:05,350
I'M TRYING TO REMAIN CALM--
DON'T TRIP.

243
00:09:05,350 --> 00:09:06,751
YOU KNOW,
THIS IS THE BUSINESS.

244
00:09:06,751 --> 00:09:10,555
JUST, YOU KNOW, GO ALONG
WITH IT, BUT I'M DISTURBED.

245
00:09:15,927 --> 00:09:18,263
(phone rings)

246
00:09:18,263 --> 00:09:19,597
HEY, MAMA.

247
00:09:19,597 --> 00:09:20,932
I HAD TO GO HOME
AND CALL MAMA.

248
00:09:20,932 --> 00:09:22,567
SHE IS MY STRENGTH.

249
00:09:22,567 --> 00:09:24,869
WHEN I'M TRIPPIN', I ALWAYS KNOW
THAT I CAN CALL MY MOM.

250
00:09:24,869 --> 00:09:27,905
IT'S TAKEN ME SO LONG TO BECOME
COMFORTABLE WITH MY GAP,

251
00:09:27,905 --> 00:09:29,641
AND, SO, I'M PISSED OFF,
BECAUSE IT'S EITHER,

252
00:09:29,641 --> 00:09:30,975
"YOU CLOSE
YOUR GAP OR YOU GO HOME."

253
00:09:30,975 --> 00:09:32,910
Uh-huh.

254
00:09:37,615 --> 00:09:38,549
SO YOU'RE NOT READY
TO CUT YOUR HAIR?

255
00:09:38,549 --> 00:09:39,717
NO.

256
00:09:39,717 --> 00:09:41,586
YOU JUST GOTTA LEAVE MY SET,
OKAY?

257
00:09:45,223 --> 00:09:46,958
I HAD TO THINK ABOUT IT.

258
00:09:46,958 --> 00:09:49,894
IT'S LIKE, OKAY, DO I LIKE MY
GAP MORE THAN I LIKE MODELING?

259
00:10:04,459 --> 00:10:09,280
♪♪♪

260
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:12,283
MISS TYRA BANKS WANTED ME
TO GO BACK TO THE DENTIST

261
00:10:12,283 --> 00:10:13,985
TO GET MY GAP CLOSED.

262
00:10:13,985 --> 00:10:16,287
DO I DO IT
OR DO I NOT DO IT?

263
00:10:16,287 --> 00:10:19,190
SO WE TALKED A LITTLE BIT
ABOUT THE--ABOUT THE GAP

264
00:10:19,190 --> 00:10:20,958
BETWEEN YOUR TWO FRONT TEETH.

265
00:10:20,958 --> 00:10:22,927
I MAY NOT BE ABLE
TO SHUT IT COMPLETELY,

266
00:10:22,927 --> 00:10:24,462
BUT LET'S SEE IF WE CAN REACH
A HAPPY MEDIUM

267
00:10:24,462 --> 00:10:26,831
AND GET SOMETHING
THAT STILL LOOKS NATURAL.

268
00:10:26,831 --> 00:10:28,966
I DON'T WANNA BE, LIKE,
ASHAMED TO SMILE, BECAUSE--

269
00:10:28,966 --> 00:10:30,435
NO, NO,
WELL, THAT'S NOT GONNA WORK

270
00:10:30,435 --> 00:10:31,536
FOR YOUR LINE OF WORK ANYWAY.

271
00:10:31,536 --> 00:10:33,204
- OKAY.
- WE WANNA MAKE YOU HAPPY.

272
00:10:33,204 --> 00:10:34,772
YOU KNOW, AS TYRA WOULD SAY,
WE WANT YOU TO LOOK FIERCE.

273
00:10:34,772 --> 00:10:35,773
RIGHT.

274
00:10:35,773 --> 00:10:37,208
I DO RESPECT TYRA'S OPINION.

275
00:10:37,208 --> 00:10:39,143
I DO TAKE HEED TO EVERYTHING
THAT SHE'S SAYIN'.

276
00:10:39,143 --> 00:10:41,379
SO I GOTTA SUCK IT UP,
I GOTTA BITE MY LIP,

277
00:10:41,379 --> 00:10:44,415
AND I GOTTA GET MY GAP CLOSED,
AS MUCH AS I DON'T WANT TO.

278
00:10:44,415 --> 00:10:52,357
♪♪♪

279
00:10:56,027 --> 00:10:57,295
THAT'S US BEFORE THERE.

280
00:10:57,295 --> 00:10:58,529
THIS IS WHAT YOU GOT NOW.

281
00:10:58,529 --> 00:11:00,264
(gasps)
OH, MY GOODNESS.

282
00:11:00,264 --> 00:11:01,866
SO WE DIDN'T
CLOSE IT DOWN ALL THE WAY.

283
00:11:01,866 --> 00:11:02,834
IF WE CLOSE IT DOWN
ALL THE WAY,

284
00:11:02,834 --> 00:11:04,435
IT WILL MAKE THEM LOOK, UH...

285
00:11:04,435 --> 00:11:05,903
LIKE CHEATING.

286
00:11:05,903 --> 00:11:07,105
ARE YOU HAPPY
WITH THE WAY IT LOOKS?

287
00:11:07,105 --> 00:11:08,439
YEAH, YOU DID A GOOD JOB.

288
00:11:08,439 --> 00:11:10,041
I LIKE IT, KIND OF.

289
00:11:10,041 --> 00:11:11,376
IT'S DIFFERENT.

290
00:11:11,376 --> 00:11:12,844
IT'S GONNA TAKE ME
SOME GETTIN' USED TO.

291
00:11:12,844 --> 00:11:14,379
I'M GONNA BE IN THE MIRROR
ALL NIGHT TONIGHT.

292
00:11:14,379 --> 00:11:16,314
IT'S SO WEIRD
HAVING THE GAP CLOSED.

293
00:11:16,314 --> 00:11:18,349
I MEAN, IT'S BEEN A PART OF ME,
LIKE, ALL MY LIFE,

294
00:11:18,349 --> 00:11:20,084
AND NOW IT'S NOT THERE ANYMORE,
BUT, YOU KNOW, I'M GONNA

295
00:11:20,084 --> 00:11:21,986
KEEP A SMILE ON MY FACE
AND KEEP GOIN'.

296
00:11:21,986 --> 00:11:24,522
♪♪♪

297
00:11:24,522 --> 00:11:26,891
THERE WAS A STUPID CHALLENGE.

298
00:11:26,891 --> 00:11:30,762
HE DIDN'T GET THE IMPRESSION
THAT I--THIS IS, LIKE,

299
00:11:30,762 --> 00:11:32,463
REALLY WHAT I WANNA BE DOING.

300
00:11:32,463 --> 00:11:35,900
I THINK THE FACT THAT
I WAS KIND OF FOUND IN A MALL

301
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:37,969
HAS WORKED AGAINST ME ALMOST.

302
00:11:37,969 --> 00:11:40,972
SO SARA, WE FOUND YOU
IN A MALL AND CHASED YOU DOWN.

303
00:11:40,972 --> 00:11:42,373
I'VE ALWAYS WONDERED
ABOUT MODELING.

304
00:11:42,373 --> 00:11:43,474
I'VE BEEN APPROACHED
IN THE PAST,

305
00:11:43,474 --> 00:11:45,009
BUT I'VE ALWAYS
BEEN AN ATHLETE.

306
00:11:45,009 --> 00:11:48,079
MY DESIRE HAS BEEN QUESTIONED,
LIKE, NUMEROUS TIMES,

307
00:11:48,079 --> 00:11:52,049
AND I JUST--
I HATE HEARING THAT.

308
00:11:52,049 --> 00:11:53,251
I mean, you just have to

309
00:11:53,251 --> 00:11:56,020
go the extra mile with that,
you know?

310
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:58,389
I DON'T WANT PEOPLE TO THINK
THAT I DON'T WANNA BE HERE.

311
00:11:58,389 --> 00:12:01,058
I REALLY NEED TO SHOW
HOW MUCH I DO WANT IT.

312
00:12:01,058 --> 00:12:08,065
♪♪♪

313
00:12:08,065 --> 00:12:09,500
WE WERE SUPPOSED
TO BE HAVING DINNER,

314
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:14,372
AND WE WALK INTO THIS ROOM,
AND IT LOOKS VERY CULTURAL.

315
00:12:14,372 --> 00:12:17,241
ALL OF A SUDDEN, WE HEAR
SOME HIGH HEELS CLICKING.

316
00:12:17,241 --> 00:12:18,976
HI, GIRLS.

317
00:12:18,976 --> 00:12:20,311
I'M TY-RA.

318
00:12:20,311 --> 00:12:22,046
(screaming)

319
00:12:22,046 --> 00:12:25,349
IN COMES A FAKE
DRAG QUEEN VERSION OF TYRA.

320
00:12:25,349 --> 00:12:26,417
(laughs)

321
00:12:26,417 --> 00:12:28,152
I JUST WANTED TO COME IN

322
00:12:28,152 --> 00:12:29,954
AND HAVE A LITTLE CHIT-CHAT
WITH YOU GIRLS.

323
00:12:29,954 --> 00:12:32,890
AND IT'S SUTAN,
OUR MAKEUP ARTIST.

324
00:12:32,890 --> 00:12:34,292
EVERY MORNING WHEN I WAKE UP,

325
00:12:34,292 --> 00:12:36,093
LITTLE WOODLAND ANIMALS
COME TO GREET ME.

326
00:12:36,093 --> 00:12:37,462
(laughs)

327
00:12:37,462 --> 00:12:39,197
- I'M TY-RA.
- TY-RA.

328
00:12:39,197 --> 00:12:40,498
I'M TY-RA.
CAN'T YOU TELL?

329
00:12:40,498 --> 00:12:43,434
LOOK, I GOT THE OUTFIT ON.
I'M TYRA, HEY, HONEY.

330
00:12:43,434 --> 00:12:44,502
YOU KNOW WHAT?

331
00:12:44,502 --> 00:12:47,004
(screams)

332
00:12:47,004 --> 00:12:49,841
I AM SO TIRED
OF YOU IMPERSONATING ME.

333
00:12:49,841 --> 00:12:51,275
AM I TY-RA?
I'M TY-RA.

334
00:12:51,275 --> 00:12:52,510
- TYRA.
- THANK YOU.

335
00:12:52,510 --> 00:12:54,912
- I'M TY-RA.
- I AM TYRA.

336
00:12:54,912 --> 00:12:57,815
- I AM TY-RA.
- I AM TY. TY TY, BABY.

337
00:12:57,815 --> 00:12:59,984
- I'M TY.
- YOU KNOW WHAT?

338
00:12:59,984 --> 00:13:01,052
I THINK THE ONLY WAY WE'RE GONNA
BE ABLE TO SETTLE THIS

339
00:13:01,052 --> 00:13:02,353
IS TO GO TO THAILAND!

340
00:13:02,353 --> 00:13:08,426
(screaming)

341
00:13:08,426 --> 00:13:11,028
A COUPLE MINUTES AGO,
I WAS DEPRESSED ABOUT THE GAP.

342
00:13:11,028 --> 00:13:13,264
I'M LIKE,
"FORGET THE GAP, SUCKA.

343
00:13:13,264 --> 00:13:15,032
I'M GOIN' TO THAILAND."

344
00:13:15,032 --> 00:13:17,268
THAILAND HAS
A WHOLE BUNCH OF FASHION

345
00:13:17,268 --> 00:13:19,270
THAT YOU WOULD NOT BELIEVE.

346
00:13:19,270 --> 00:13:21,239
THEY HAVE THAI FASHION WEEK.

347
00:13:21,239 --> 00:13:23,007
IT'S CALLED
"EL BANGKOK FASHION WEEK,"

348
00:13:23,007 --> 00:13:27,512
AND THE NEXT TIME I SEE YOU
IS GOING TO BE IN THAILAND.

349
00:13:27,512 --> 00:13:28,880
SO I'LL SEE YOU LATER.

350
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:29,947
(screaming)

351
00:13:29,947 --> 00:13:31,482
I'LL SEE YOU LATER!

352
00:13:31,482 --> 00:13:34,452
I DON'T KNOW IF THAILAND
IS READY FOR FURONDA YET.

353
00:13:34,452 --> 00:13:36,087
THEY'D BETTER BRACE
THEMSELVES.

354
00:13:36,087 --> 00:13:37,822
I'VE ONLY BEEN TO CANADA.
THAT'S IT.

355
00:13:37,822 --> 00:13:41,792
♪♪♪

356
00:13:41,792 --> 00:13:45,263
WE ARE GOING TO THAILAND!
WHAT?!

357
00:13:45,263 --> 00:13:46,097
THIS IS YOU.

358
00:13:46,097 --> 00:13:47,999
YES.

359
00:13:47,999 --> 00:13:50,334
MOVIN' OUT OF OUR HOUSE
IN L.A. IS BITTERSWEET.

360
00:13:50,334 --> 00:13:51,536
SO MANY MEMORIES HERE--

361
00:13:51,536 --> 00:13:53,804
THE ARGUMENTS WE HAD,
THE MAKE-UPS.

362
00:13:53,804 --> 00:13:55,506
NOW THAT
IT'S ONLY DOWN TO SIX,

363
00:13:55,506 --> 00:13:57,475
YOU REALLY DON'T KNOW NOW

364
00:13:57,475 --> 00:14:00,311
WHAT COULD BE
THE DECIDING FACTOR.

365
00:14:00,311 --> 00:14:05,750
IT'S REALLY A TIME
YOU REALLY HAVE TO STEP IT UP.

366
00:14:05,750 --> 00:14:07,118
OH.

367
00:14:07,118 --> 00:14:08,452
BYE, HOUSE.

368
00:14:08,452 --> 00:14:10,321
IT WAS NICE KNOWING YOU.

369
00:14:10,321 --> 00:14:13,457
I DON'T KNOW WHAT'S GONNA BE IN
STORE WHEN WE GET TO THAILAND,

370
00:14:13,457 --> 00:14:16,060
BUT I HAVE
HIGH EXPECTATIONS OF MYSELF,

371
00:14:16,060 --> 00:14:20,331
AND I THINK OTHER PEOPLE HAVE
HIGH EXPECTATIONS OF ME, TOO.

372
00:14:20,331 --> 00:14:23,134
NNENNA IS ONE
OF MY MAIN COMPETITORS,

373
00:14:23,134 --> 00:14:24,302
SO I'M JUST GONNA
HAVE TO WORK HARDER

374
00:14:24,302 --> 00:14:25,803
'CAUSE I WANNA WIN,

375
00:14:25,803 --> 00:14:28,039
AND I DON'T WANT ANYBODY ELSE
TO WIN OVER ME.

376
00:14:28,039 --> 00:14:33,778
♪♪♪

377
00:14:54,065 --> 00:14:56,434
I CANNOT BELIEVE
I'M IN BANGKOK, THAILAND.

378
00:14:56,434 --> 00:14:58,269
I CAN'T BELIEVE IT.

379
00:14:58,269 --> 00:15:01,505
WE ARRIVED IN BANGKOK,
AND UP PULLS A PINK VAN.

380
00:15:01,505 --> 00:15:08,279
♪♪♪

381
00:15:08,279 --> 00:15:10,848
I'VE NEVER SEEN
ANYTHING LIKE THIS VAN BEFORE.

382
00:15:10,848 --> 00:15:16,287
SO WE HOP INTO OUR NEW CAR
AND TAKE OFF TO THE UNKNOWN.

383
00:15:16,287 --> 00:15:19,123
♪♪♪

384
00:15:19,123 --> 00:15:22,059
SAWADEE...
SAWADEE KAH.

385
00:15:22,059 --> 00:15:24,462
WE'RE TRYING TO MAKE
A GOOD IMPRESSION HERE

386
00:15:24,462 --> 00:15:26,897
AND POSSIBLY WORK HERE
IN THE FUTURE.

387
00:15:26,897 --> 00:15:30,067
SO, UM, IT'S VERY IMPORTANT
TO LEARN THEIR CULTURE.

388
00:15:30,067 --> 00:15:31,836
WE LEARNED A BUNCH OF STUFF
ON THE PLANE.

389
00:15:31,836 --> 00:15:34,005
HELLO...
SAWADEE KAH.

390
00:15:34,005 --> 00:15:34,939
HOW MUCH?
HOW DO YOU SAY, "HOW MUCH?"

391
00:15:34,939 --> 00:15:36,207
HOW MUCH IS...

392
00:15:36,207 --> 00:15:37,541
TAU RAI?

393
00:15:37,541 --> 00:15:38,909
TAU RAI?
HOW DO YOU SAY "TOO MUCH?"

394
00:15:38,909 --> 00:15:40,244
TOO MUCH?

395
00:15:40,244 --> 00:15:41,512
TOO MUCH?
JUST SAY, "NO, THANK YOU."

396
00:15:41,512 --> 00:15:43,981
I CANNOT WAIT TO SHOP,

397
00:15:43,981 --> 00:15:46,150
BECAUSE I HAVE
ABOUT 3,000 BAHT,

398
00:15:46,150 --> 00:15:49,420
AND I'M GONNA
SPEND IT ALL HERE.

399
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:52,490
(speaks Thai)

400
00:15:54,025 --> 00:15:55,359
WHEN WE ARRIVED
AT OUR HOTEL,

401
00:15:55,359 --> 00:15:57,762
WE ARE JUST BLOWN AWAY.

402
00:15:57,762 --> 00:15:58,496
THIS IS WHERE WE'RE STAYIN'?

403
00:15:58,496 --> 00:16:00,831
NO WAY.

404
00:16:00,831 --> 00:16:02,333
MM.

405
00:16:02,333 --> 00:16:04,201
IT TAKES YOUR BREATH AWAY
HOW BEAUTIFUL IT IS.

406
00:16:04,201 --> 00:16:05,936
AH...
SAWADEE KAH.

407
00:16:05,936 --> 00:16:07,872
OH, THANK YOU.
CHEERS, EVERYBODY.

408
00:16:07,872 --> 00:16:09,440
CHEERS TO EVERYONE.

409
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:11,542
CHEERS.

410
00:16:13,144 --> 00:16:16,347
WHOO!

411
00:16:16,347 --> 00:16:18,449
OH, MY GOODNESS.

412
00:16:18,449 --> 00:16:21,318
WHAT A SPECTACULAR HOTEL.

413
00:16:21,318 --> 00:16:24,088
IT IS FIT FOR A KING,
BUT WE ARE QUEENS,

414
00:16:24,088 --> 00:16:26,757
AND IT DEFINITELY
SUITS US TO A "T."

415
00:16:26,757 --> 00:16:29,193
LOOK AT THIS.

416
00:16:29,193 --> 00:16:30,761
LOOK IT--
JADE, YOU WEREN'T KIDDING.

417
00:16:30,761 --> 00:16:33,097
THAT IS ABSOLUTELY GORGEOUS.

418
00:16:33,097 --> 00:16:35,266
OH, MY GOD.

419
00:16:35,266 --> 00:16:36,967
LOOK IN HERE.

420
00:16:36,967 --> 00:16:39,537
OH, YOU GUYS HAVE
A NICE BATHROOM.

421
00:16:39,537 --> 00:16:41,205
SWEET.

422
00:16:41,205 --> 00:16:42,239
LOOK AT THIS.

423
00:16:42,239 --> 00:16:44,308
IT'S REAL, TOO.

424
00:16:44,308 --> 00:16:46,510
"STOP, GO AWAY,
I'M LOST, HELP."

425
00:16:46,510 --> 00:16:47,945
(laughs)
"GO AWAY."

426
00:16:47,945 --> 00:16:51,182
(laughs)
WHAT KIND OF NONSENSE?

427
00:16:51,182 --> 00:16:53,350
BEING A TOP MODEL,
YOU'RE GONNA TRAVEL THE WORLD.

428
00:16:53,350 --> 00:16:56,287
I THINK THIS IS A GREAT TEST
FOR ALL OF US TO SEE

429
00:16:56,287 --> 00:16:59,056
WHO CAN REALLY HANDLE
THE CULTURE SHOCK.

430
00:16:59,056 --> 00:17:00,991
ARE YOU SURE?
(speaks Thai)

431
00:17:00,991 --> 00:17:05,496
♪♪♪

432
00:17:05,496 --> 00:17:09,233
WE ARRIVE AT THE DULAYA SPA
TO PAMPER JADE AND NNENNA.

433
00:17:09,233 --> 00:17:11,268
NNENNA WON
THE INTERVIEW CHALLENGE.

434
00:17:11,268 --> 00:17:12,269
I'M GONNA GO WITH NNENNA.

435
00:17:12,269 --> 00:17:13,471
(applause)

436
00:17:13,471 --> 00:17:15,905
SHE CHOSE JADE
TO JOIN IN HER SPA TREATMENT.

437
00:17:15,905 --> 00:17:18,375
WELCOME TO DULAYA SPA.

438
00:17:18,375 --> 00:17:21,679
WHO ARE THE LUCKY LADIES
WHO HAVE WON THE SPECIAL PRIZE?

439
00:17:21,679 --> 00:17:23,814
OKAY, WELCOME, PLEASE.

440
00:17:23,814 --> 00:17:27,418
SO FAR IN THE COMPETITION,
I'VE WON MOST OF THE CHALLENGES.

441
00:17:27,418 --> 00:17:29,386
IT'S GOOD TO BE DOING WELL.

442
00:17:29,386 --> 00:17:31,055
I'M NOT JUST ONE OF THE BUNCH.

443
00:17:31,055 --> 00:17:33,124
I'M ACTUALLY DOIN' OUTSTANDIN'.

444
00:17:33,124 --> 00:17:35,626
AND THE OTHER LADIES,
PLEASE COME FOLLOW ME, PLEASE.

445
00:17:35,626 --> 00:17:37,027
FURONDA AND JOANIE

446
00:17:37,027 --> 00:17:39,697
ARE GOING TO BE ASSISTING
WITH THE MASSAGES.

447
00:17:39,697 --> 00:17:41,599
FOR THE FIRST, WE WILL TAKE
THE BODY SCRUB

448
00:17:41,599 --> 00:17:42,900
FOR THE WINNER FIRST.

449
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:44,135
THEY'RE GONNA BE NAKED?

450
00:17:44,135 --> 00:17:46,937
DANIELLE AND I ARE GOING
TO BE ASSISTING THE GIRLS

451
00:17:46,937 --> 00:17:48,539
WITH THEIR BATHS.

452
00:17:52,109 --> 00:17:53,077
OH, GOT IT.

453
00:18:03,354 --> 00:18:07,691
I FEEL KINDA BAD, BECAUSE I
REALLY WAS NOT DOIN' MY JOB.

454
00:18:07,691 --> 00:18:09,160
I STRAIGHT FAILED.

455
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:11,796
I COULD HAVE DONE A BETTER JOB,
BUT I'M EXHAUSTED RIGHT NOW.

456
00:18:11,796 --> 00:18:13,531
(humming)

457
00:18:13,531 --> 00:18:17,568
I AM TAKING THIS,
UH, RESPONSIBILITY SERIOUSLY

458
00:18:17,568 --> 00:18:19,670
BECAUSE OF THE CULTURE HERE.

459
00:18:19,670 --> 00:18:21,105
CAN YOU DEMONSTRATE
ON THIS LEG FOR ME?

460
00:18:21,105 --> 00:18:22,873
SHOW ME.

461
00:18:22,873 --> 00:18:25,709
I DON'T WORK WELL WITH BODIES
AND TOUCHIN' ON PEOPLE,

462
00:18:25,709 --> 00:18:26,844
FEELIN' 'EM.

463
00:18:26,844 --> 00:18:28,479
I DON'T DO WELL WITH THAT.

464
00:18:28,479 --> 00:18:30,080
I'M A MODEL,
NOT A MASSEUSE.

465
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:32,449
♪♪♪

466
00:18:32,449 --> 00:18:35,419
FURONDA WAS MASSAGING
NNENNA'S LEG WITH ONE FINGER.

467
00:18:35,419 --> 00:18:37,488
HOW YOU GONNA MASSAGE OIL IN
WITH ONE FINGER?

468
00:18:37,488 --> 00:18:38,856
DON'T THAT FEEL GOOD,
NNENNA?

469
00:18:38,856 --> 00:18:42,626
I FEEL LIKE
YOU'RE SCRATCHIN' ME, FURONDA.

470
00:18:42,626 --> 00:18:44,762
THIS IS MY MASSAGE.
THIS IS WHAT YOU GET.

471
00:18:44,762 --> 00:18:45,996
I DON'T HAVE
AN ITCH, FURONDA.

472
00:18:45,996 --> 00:18:48,465
(laughs)
STOP IT.

473
00:18:48,465 --> 00:18:50,067
(laughs)

474
00:18:50,067 --> 00:18:53,704
WE'RE IN A COUNTRY
WHERE RESPECT IS SO IMPORTANT,

475
00:18:53,704 --> 00:18:55,573
AND WE GOTTA JUST
TOUGH IT OUT,

476
00:18:55,573 --> 00:18:56,974
AND YOU HAVE TO DO YOUR BEST
NO MATTER WHAT.

477
00:18:59,810 --> 00:19:01,579
YOU WANNA DO THESE?

478
00:19:01,579 --> 00:19:03,848
JOANIE, YOU DON'T HAVE ANY KIDS
HERE, ESPECIALLY NOT ME.

479
00:19:03,848 --> 00:19:05,482
I'M GROWN, OKAY?

480
00:19:05,482 --> 00:19:06,817
DID YOU--DO YOU WANNA
TAKE OVER?

481
00:19:06,817 --> 00:19:08,185
NO.

482
00:19:08,185 --> 00:19:10,621
OKAY, WELL, GO BACK THERE
AND MIND YOUR OWN BUSINESS.

483
00:19:10,621 --> 00:19:12,590
I WOULD APPRECIATE IT.
THANK YOU.

484
00:19:12,590 --> 00:19:15,926
FURONDA
IS DOING HER OWN THING.

485
00:19:15,926 --> 00:19:18,996
JUST NOT GIVING A RAT'S ASS
ABOUT IT, REALLY.

486
00:19:18,996 --> 00:19:20,397
ANYTHING ELSE?

487
00:19:20,397 --> 00:19:21,765
NO, THAT'S IT, THANK YOU.

488
00:19:21,765 --> 00:19:23,367
CAN I GET MY TIP, NNENNA?

489
00:19:23,367 --> 00:19:24,735
WHERE YOUR PURSE AT?
I'LL JUST GET IT OUT MYSELF.

490
00:19:24,735 --> 00:19:26,403
OKAY.

491
00:19:26,403 --> 00:19:27,605
I'M SO GLAD THAT'S BEHIND ME.

492
00:19:27,605 --> 00:19:28,806
I CAN GO AND WASH MY FINGER
AND TRY TO...

493
00:19:28,806 --> 00:19:30,441
(breathes deeply)
SNAP OUT OF IT.

494
00:19:33,978 --> 00:19:35,946
CAN YOU TURN THE AIR OFF,
PLEASE?

495
00:19:40,044 --> 00:19:41,730
♪♪♪

496
00:19:41,730 --> 00:19:42,731
TYRA MAIL!

497
00:19:42,731 --> 00:19:44,633
TYRA MAIL.

498
00:19:44,633 --> 00:19:46,635
"I KNOW IT'S TOUGH
BEING AROUND SO MANY GIRLS.

499
00:19:46,635 --> 00:19:48,870
SO GET SOME TAIL.
TYRA."

500
00:19:48,870 --> 00:19:50,372
I WISH.
(laughs)

501
00:19:50,372 --> 00:19:51,673
WE GONNA BE AROUND GUYS?

502
00:19:51,673 --> 00:19:52,841
NO, IT'S SOMETHING
WITH ANIMALS.

503
00:19:52,841 --> 00:19:54,476
"GET SOME TAIL"?

504
00:19:54,476 --> 00:19:56,511
WHAT IS TYRA BANKS
TALKING ABOUT, "GET SOME TAIL"?

505
00:19:56,511 --> 00:19:57,679
I'M CURIOUS AS TO FIND OUT

506
00:19:57,679 --> 00:19:59,414
WHAT KIND OF TAIL
WE GONNA BE GETTING.

507
00:19:59,414 --> 00:20:01,550
WHAT IS IT GONNA BE?

508
00:20:01,550 --> 00:20:09,257
♪♪♪

509
00:20:16,498 --> 00:20:17,766
SO WE ARRIVE
AT THE PHOTO SHOOT,

510
00:20:17,766 --> 00:20:19,534
AND WE SEE THESE WOMEN

511
00:20:19,534 --> 00:20:21,470
AND THEY HAVE
FRUITS AND VEGETABLES,

512
00:20:21,470 --> 00:20:23,839
AND THEY'RE JUST FLOATING
IN THIS CANAL.

513
00:20:23,839 --> 00:20:26,708
JUST...
CHILLIN'.

514
00:20:26,708 --> 00:20:28,143
SO HOW ARE YOU GUYS
THIS MORNING?

515
00:20:28,143 --> 00:20:29,511
GREAT.

516
00:20:29,511 --> 00:20:31,213
SO THIS IS OUR FIRST
PHOTO SHOOT IN THAILAND.

517
00:20:31,213 --> 00:20:32,614
- ARE YOU GUYS PSYCHED?
- YEAH.

518
00:20:32,614 --> 00:20:34,816
SO TODAY YOU GIRLS
ARE GONNA BE SHOOTING HERE

519
00:20:34,816 --> 00:20:37,719
IN THE FAMOUS FLOATING MARKET
IN THAILAND.

520
00:20:37,719 --> 00:20:40,288
THIS IS WHERE YOU CAN COME BUY
FRUITS AND VEGETABLES AND FISH.

521
00:20:40,288 --> 00:20:43,425
AND TODAY YOU GIRLS ARE GONNA
BE THE CATCH OF THE DAY,

522
00:20:43,425 --> 00:20:46,661
AS IF WE ARE FISHING YOU
OUT OF THIS WATERWAY.

523
00:20:46,661 --> 00:20:49,331
BEHIND ME, YOU CAN SEE
THERE IS A BIG RIGGING

524
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:50,565
WHERE YOU GIRLS
ARE GONNA BE HOISTED UP

525
00:20:50,565 --> 00:20:52,467
AND HUNG UPSIDE DOWN.

526
00:20:52,467 --> 00:20:54,569
AND YOU'RE ACTUALLY
GONNA BE MERMAIDS,

527
00:20:54,569 --> 00:20:56,238
SO IT'S GONNA BE A REALLY,
REALLY COOL SHOOT.

528
00:20:56,238 --> 00:20:59,341
NOW TODAY'S SHOOT IS FOR
BANANA BOAT SUNTAN LOTION,

529
00:20:59,341 --> 00:21:01,743
AND BANANA BOAT WANTS YOU
TO CELEBRATE THE SUN

530
00:21:01,743 --> 00:21:03,412
WITH THEIR ANTI-BURN SYSTEM.

531
00:21:03,412 --> 00:21:05,380
SINCE YOU'RE GONNA
BE OUTSIDE ALL DAY,

532
00:21:05,380 --> 00:21:07,149
DON'T FORGET
TO PUT ON YOUR BANANA BOAT

533
00:21:07,149 --> 00:21:08,417
BEFORE YOU
GET IN THE HARNESS.

534
00:21:08,417 --> 00:21:10,318
YOUR PHOTOGRAPHER
TODAY IS NOOM.

535
00:21:10,318 --> 00:21:11,853
NOOM, COME OVER HERE.

536
00:21:11,853 --> 00:21:13,855
HE'S AN AMAZING
FASHION PHOTOGRAPHER.

537
00:21:13,855 --> 00:21:15,557
THESE ARE YOU
SIX VICTIMS TODAY.

538
00:21:15,557 --> 00:21:17,092
YEAH, YEAH.

539
00:21:17,092 --> 00:21:18,627
ALL RIGHT?
SO LET'S GO DO THE SHOOT.

540
00:21:18,627 --> 00:21:19,761
LET'S GO!

541
00:21:19,761 --> 00:21:27,702
♪♪♪

542
00:21:34,843 --> 00:21:38,280
WE'RE GONNA BRING YOU SOME
LITTLE FISH AND SOME SEAWEED,

543
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:40,449
'CAUSE IF YOU WERE SCOOPED
OUT OF THE WATER,

544
00:21:40,449 --> 00:21:42,284
THERE'D BE SOME FISH
IN THAT NET, TOO.

545
00:21:42,284 --> 00:21:44,586
IS THAT FISH JUICE
THAT I JUST FELT?

546
00:21:44,586 --> 00:21:46,254
I REALLY HOPE THERE ARE NOT
ANY PIRANHAS IN THERE,

547
00:21:46,254 --> 00:21:48,156
'CAUSE WE HAVE DEAD FISH
ATTACHED TO US.

548
00:21:48,156 --> 00:21:49,324
(groans)

549
00:21:49,324 --> 00:21:50,826
IF A PIRANHA
START BITING ON MY NECK,

550
00:21:50,826 --> 00:21:52,594
I'MA BE A MAD SISTER.

551
00:21:52,594 --> 00:21:58,333
♪♪♪

552
00:21:58,333 --> 00:21:59,334
(speaking Thai)

553
00:21:59,334 --> 00:22:00,535
HOW'S IT SMELL, DANIELLE?

554
00:22:00,535 --> 00:22:02,437
I JUST THREW UP IN MY MOUTH
A LITTLE BIT.

555
00:22:02,437 --> 00:22:03,839
(laughter)

556
00:22:03,839 --> 00:22:06,475
SO THE IDEA OF THE SHOOT
IS YOU'RE KINDA UPSIDE DOWN.

557
00:22:06,475 --> 00:22:07,509
OKAY?

558
00:22:07,509 --> 00:22:08,743
UGH!

559
00:22:08,743 --> 00:22:10,278
FISH JUICE.

560
00:22:10,278 --> 00:22:11,279
FISH JUICE?

561
00:22:11,279 --> 00:22:12,747
WORK WITH IT, GIRL!

562
00:22:12,747 --> 00:22:14,149
NOW POSE.

563
00:22:14,149 --> 00:22:15,383
YES.

564
00:22:15,383 --> 00:22:17,219
THAT'S A PRETTY ONE,
DANIELLE.

565
00:22:17,219 --> 00:22:19,321
I LIKE HOW
YOU'RE USING YOUR HANDS.

566
00:22:19,321 --> 00:22:20,589
I'M FEELING SO MUCH PAIN
RIGHT NOW.

567
00:22:20,589 --> 00:22:22,224
THE HARNESS IS, LIKE,
GETTING TIGHTER,

568
00:22:22,224 --> 00:22:25,494
SO MY UTERUS IS, UH, PROBABLY
FLAT AS A PANCAKE RIGHT NOW.

569
00:22:25,494 --> 00:22:26,761
IS IT OKAY LIKE THAT?

570
00:22:26,761 --> 00:22:29,264
CAN YOU REST THERE
OR DO YOU WANNA COME ON BACK?

571
00:22:29,264 --> 00:22:30,398
I WANNA GET 'EM DONE.
LET'S GO.

572
00:22:30,398 --> 00:22:31,433
OKAY, YOU GOT 15 MORE.

573
00:22:31,433 --> 00:22:33,168
15?

574
00:22:33,168 --> 00:22:34,769
A COUPLE TIMES, YOU KNOW,
I WAS, LIKE, "OH, MY GOD,

575
00:22:34,769 --> 00:22:35,770
THIS HURTS SO BAD.
I WANNA QUIT."

576
00:22:35,770 --> 00:22:37,439
CAN YOU DO IT?

577
00:22:37,439 --> 00:22:39,274
SO I HAD TO KINDA GET MYSELF
TOGETHER AND SUCK IT UP.

578
00:22:39,274 --> 00:22:40,675
I'M NOT A QUITTER,
SO I HAD TO KEEP GOING.

579
00:22:40,675 --> 00:22:43,445
SHE GOES FROM THIS TO THIS...
AND SHE KNOWS HER ANGLES.

580
00:22:43,445 --> 00:22:44,880
LIKE, NOTICE HOW
SHE ANGLES HER HEAD?

581
00:22:44,880 --> 00:22:46,681
SHE KNOWS WHAT LOOKS PRETTY.

582
00:22:46,681 --> 00:22:49,417
WHEN I PUT DANIELLE OUT THERE,
I FEEL LIKE A PROUD PAPA,

583
00:22:49,417 --> 00:22:50,619
'CAUSE SHE KNOWS
WHAT SHE'S DOING.

584
00:22:50,619 --> 00:22:52,821
OKAY, GOOD JOB, DANIELLE.

585
00:22:52,821 --> 00:22:54,756
NEXT VICTIM.

586
00:22:56,858 --> 00:22:59,261
NNENNA,
IF YOU PUSH ON YOUR HIPS,

587
00:22:59,261 --> 00:23:01,329
IT'LL STRAIGHTEN YOU OUT
A LITTLE MORE.

588
00:23:01,329 --> 00:23:02,831
DON'T HOLD ONTO THAT CORD
THOUGH,

589
00:23:02,831 --> 00:23:04,533
'CAUSE WE'RE
RETOUCHING THAT OUT.

590
00:23:04,533 --> 00:23:06,835
IT'S DIFFICULT BECAUSE WHEN
I PICTURE A MERMAID,

591
00:23:06,835 --> 00:23:09,871
I PICTURE,
LIKE, LONG, NICE HAIR,

592
00:23:09,871 --> 00:23:12,374
AND I DIDN'T HAVE
ANY HAIR EXTENSIONS,

593
00:23:12,374 --> 00:23:14,142
SO I DON'T KNOW WHAT KIND OF
OF MERMAID I WOULD LOOK LIKE.

594
00:23:14,142 --> 00:23:16,444
I NEED YOU TO BE REALLY FEMININE
ABOUT YOUR ARM MOVEMENTS.

595
00:23:16,444 --> 00:23:18,613
CAN I GET A DIFFERENT
FACIAL EXPRESSION?

596
00:23:18,613 --> 00:23:22,751
THERE YOU GO.

597
00:23:22,751 --> 00:23:25,854
NNENNA STARTED AT THE TOP AND
JUST KIND OF COASTED FROM THERE,

598
00:23:25,854 --> 00:23:28,156
BUT THIS COMPETITION
IS ABOUT IMPROVING,

599
00:23:28,156 --> 00:23:30,792
AND I DON'T NECESSARILY THINK
NNENNA'S STILL IMPROVING AT ALL.

600
00:23:30,792 --> 00:23:32,127
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT, NNENNA?

601
00:23:32,127 --> 00:23:33,528
YEAH.

602
00:23:33,528 --> 00:23:35,163
YOU HAVE TO JUST PUSH THROUGH
TEN MORE FRAMES,

603
00:23:35,163 --> 00:23:36,698
AND THEN YOU'RE DONE.

604
00:23:36,698 --> 00:23:39,534
THIS IS CUTTING OFF
MY CIRCULATION IN MY STOMACH.

605
00:23:39,534 --> 00:23:41,303
IF YOU TWIST YOUR HIPS
TO CAMERA,

606
00:23:41,303 --> 00:23:42,771
IT WON'T HURT AS MUCH,
TWIST.

607
00:23:42,771 --> 00:23:44,539
THERE YOU GO.

608
00:23:44,539 --> 00:23:47,475
I THINK WE ALL KINDA PUT
NNENNA UP ON THIS HIGH PEDESTAL,

609
00:23:47,475 --> 00:23:48,810
BUT SHE DIDN'T DO AS WELL

610
00:23:48,810 --> 00:23:51,146
AS I THOUGHT THAT SHE WOULD
IN THE PHOTO SHOOT.

611
00:23:51,146 --> 00:23:52,681
CHIN DOWN A BIT.
THERE YOU GO.

612
00:23:52,681 --> 00:23:54,849
OKAY, WE CAN PULL HER BACK.

613
00:23:54,849 --> 00:23:57,285
WHOO!

614
00:23:57,285 --> 00:24:00,488
PLEASE DON'T BREAK ON ME.

615
00:24:00,488 --> 00:24:02,123
PRETTY, PRETTY, PRETTY.

616
00:24:02,123 --> 00:24:03,692
OH, THAT'S SO PRETTY.

617
00:24:03,692 --> 00:24:05,293
SINCE WHEN DID YOU LEARN
HOW TO MODEL?

618
00:24:05,293 --> 00:24:06,728
WHEN DID YOU LEARN
HOW TO BECOME SOFT?

619
00:24:06,728 --> 00:24:07,596
I'M LEARNING, JAY.

620
00:24:07,596 --> 00:24:09,364
HUH?

621
00:24:09,364 --> 00:24:11,333
I'M LISTENING, I'M WATCHING
AND I'M LEARNING.

622
00:24:11,333 --> 00:24:12,567
OH.
OKAY.

623
00:24:12,567 --> 00:24:14,436
FOR SOME REASON, I KEEP
ON LANDING IN THE BOTTOM TWO,

624
00:24:14,436 --> 00:24:15,704
WHICH I DON'T UNDERSTAND WHY.

625
00:24:15,704 --> 00:24:17,272
BUT I KEEP COMING BACK,

626
00:24:17,272 --> 00:24:18,273
AND I'M COMING BACK
WITH A VENGEANCE.

627
00:24:18,273 --> 00:24:19,574
I'M COMING BACK STRONG.

628
00:24:19,574 --> 00:24:21,876
NOW GIVE ME THAT SOFT FACE,
THAT LITTLE SMILE.

629
00:24:21,876 --> 00:24:23,545
JADE WAS ALWAYS SO HARD.

630
00:24:23,545 --> 00:24:25,313
NOW JADE KNOWS HOW
TO LOOK SOFT.

631
00:24:25,313 --> 00:24:29,851
AND UPSIDE DOWN,
THAT'S REAL DIFFICULT.

632
00:24:29,851 --> 00:24:32,587
GOOD JOB, JADE.
I'M IMPRESSED.

633
00:24:32,587 --> 00:24:34,389
TRY AND GET A BIT OF A SMILE
IN THERE IF YOU CAN,

634
00:24:34,389 --> 00:24:36,858
LIKE IT'S NOT 180 DEGREES
OUT HERE.

635
00:24:36,858 --> 00:24:38,627
AND POINT YOUR HEAD DOWN,
KIND OF LIKE...

636
00:24:38,627 --> 00:24:39,628
READY?
OH.

637
00:24:39,628 --> 00:24:41,229
OKAY, ONE MORE.

638
00:24:41,229 --> 00:24:43,331
WHEN YOU PUT YOUR HANDS JUST
OUT LIKE THAT, IT LOOKS LIKE

639
00:24:43,331 --> 00:24:44,733
THEY'RE JUST HANGING THERE,

640
00:24:44,733 --> 00:24:46,635
SO TRY AND BE
A LITTLE MORE GRACEFUL.

641
00:24:46,635 --> 00:24:49,304
SARA LOOKED LIKE A SCARED GUPPY
HANGING IN A NET

642
00:24:49,304 --> 00:24:50,772
FOR HER FIRST 20 FRAMES.

643
00:24:50,772 --> 00:24:52,741
THAT'S BETTER, SARA.

644
00:24:52,741 --> 00:24:54,476
THAT'S GOOD, SARA.

645
00:24:54,476 --> 00:24:56,244
BUT, YOU KNOW,
AFTER SHE GOT IT TOGETHER,

646
00:24:56,244 --> 00:24:58,413
SARA STARTED LOOKING LIKE
A MODEL.

647
00:24:58,413 --> 00:24:59,547
ARCH ALL THE WAY DOWN
LIKE THAT.

648
00:24:59,547 --> 00:25:01,149
LIKE, ALL THE WAY
YOU WERE GONNA HANG.

649
00:25:01,149 --> 00:25:02,651
STRAIGHTEN YOUR LEGS.

650
00:25:02,651 --> 00:25:04,853
HANG YOUR ARM
ALL THE WAY DOWN IF YOU CAN.

651
00:25:04,853 --> 00:25:06,788
YES, YES, YES, YES!
BEAUTIFUL.

652
00:25:06,788 --> 00:25:08,456
REALLY PRETTY AT THE END.

653
00:25:08,456 --> 00:25:10,592
I'M TRYING TO LEARN
AND GET BETTER.

654
00:25:10,592 --> 00:25:12,360
I JUST WANNA REALLY
SHOW MY DESIRE

655
00:25:12,360 --> 00:25:14,696
AND SHOW THAT
I DO WANNA BE HERE.

656
00:25:14,696 --> 00:25:16,464
OH, THAT'S REAL!

657
00:25:16,464 --> 00:25:17,866
THIS IS SO TIGHT.

658
00:25:17,866 --> 00:25:19,601
DOES IT HAVE TO BE LIKE THIS?

659
00:25:19,601 --> 00:25:23,438
THIS IS A LOT OF STUFF
TO HAVE ON.

660
00:25:23,438 --> 00:25:26,808
HI, JAY!
MR. JAY!

661
00:25:26,808 --> 00:25:28,510
WHAT ARE WE DOING?

662
00:25:28,510 --> 00:25:30,879
THE WATER'S STINKY,
THE FISH ARE NASTY

663
00:25:30,879 --> 00:25:32,781
AND I'M JUST TRYING
TO GET MY SHOOT DONE

664
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:35,183
SO I CAN
GET BACK INTO THE TRAILER,

665
00:25:35,183 --> 00:25:36,184
WHICH IS AIR-CONDITIONED.

666
00:25:36,184 --> 00:25:37,385
READY?

667
00:25:37,385 --> 00:25:38,320
I'VE BEEN
A LITTLE BIT TURNED OFF

668
00:25:38,320 --> 00:25:39,754
BY FURONDA'S DIVA ATTITUDE.

669
00:25:39,754 --> 00:25:41,623
YOU NEED TO GET OVER YOURSELF
IF YOU'RE GONNA BE IN THIS--

670
00:25:41,623 --> 00:25:42,724
IN THIS SORT OF PROFESSION.

671
00:25:42,724 --> 00:25:44,225
FURONDA, ARE YOU READY?

672
00:25:44,225 --> 00:25:45,360
LET'S GO.

673
00:25:45,360 --> 00:25:46,561
(speaks Thai)

674
00:25:46,561 --> 00:25:51,132
KEEP CHANGING UP YOUR HANDS,
FURONDA.

675
00:25:51,132 --> 00:25:52,834
THE PAIN IS SHOWING
ON YOUR FACE,

676
00:25:52,834 --> 00:25:55,170
AND I NEED YOU
TO ERASE IT FROM YOUR FACE.

677
00:25:55,170 --> 00:25:57,872
FURONDA
LOOKED LIKE FISH BAIT.

678
00:25:57,872 --> 00:26:00,108
SHE WAS SHOWING THE PAIN
ALL OVER HER FACE.

679
00:26:00,108 --> 00:26:02,344
PUT YOUR HANDS IN YOUR HAIR
IF YOU WANT.

680
00:26:02,344 --> 00:26:04,646
THERE YOU GO.
MAKE IT PRETTY.

681
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:06,715
SOFT FACE.
LOOK SERENE.

682
00:26:06,715 --> 00:26:08,817
LAST FRAME.
THERE YOU GO.

683
00:26:08,817 --> 00:26:10,452
OKAY, WE CAN PULL HER BACK.
SHE'S DONE.

684
00:26:10,452 --> 00:26:12,620
DO WE HAVE
OUR NEXT GIRL READY?

685
00:26:12,620 --> 00:26:15,623
I OWN THAT ONE, AND I HAVE
THE ONE FOR FACES, TOO.

686
00:26:15,623 --> 00:26:18,093
YOU DO?

687
00:26:18,093 --> 00:26:19,661
WHEE!

688
00:26:19,661 --> 00:26:22,464
HEY, JOANIE, TRY AND TWIST
YOUR HIPS TO CAMERA.

689
00:26:22,464 --> 00:26:24,265
I FEEL LIKE I'M GONNA
THROW UP.

690
00:26:24,265 --> 00:26:26,868
YOU FEEL LIKE
YOU'RE GONNA THROW UP?

691
00:26:26,868 --> 00:26:29,137
I JUST DRANK A LOT OF COFFEE.

